  "notes": "ECCC normals codes (annual or worst month): mean temperature A, maximum A, minimum A, precipitation C, rainfall None, snowfall None. Codes: A = WMO 3-and-5 rule met; B >= 25 years; C >= 20; D >= 15 years of complete months in the period. Composite members: VANCOUVER HARBOUR CS (1108446, 2.5 m). ECCC joins these stations into one 30-year series; climate_id is the representative ID ECCC uses for the location page. Bright sunshine is not part of the 1991–2020 normals (ECCC stopped measuring it at most sites); sunshine_h is null by source, not by omission. Not published by ECCC for this station and period (null): annual rainfall, annual snowfall. Monthly cells left blank on the ECCC page are null. Distance measured from the station to the NRCan CGNDB reference point for Vancouver (JBRIK). daylight_h_computed is computed by agent-04 from the station latitude for the 15th of each month (solar declination approximation, sunrise/sunset at -0.833°); it is not an ECCC value. extremes are the 1991–2020 normal-period extremes from the ECCC page (long-term extremes are also published there)."
